nodecode-chronos is a rewrite of DevTarlow's DevTarlow/hermes-chronos:

  https://github.com/DevTarlow/hermes-chronos
  commit 1abeae16c61d9e3939c1f29c74e81fb92299ba3f
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hermes Contender (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole of what the plugin does for a user. The shadow
repository inside the workspace is the same design -- a private git
repository under <workspace>/.nodecode-chronos/repo, driven with --git-dir
and --work-tree, a scrubbed environment, the operator's own git config kept
out of it, a .gitignore of "*" so the project's own git status stays clean,
and a checkpoint as one commit whose message carries the metadata. The four
model tools keep their names and their answers (chronos_checkpoint,
chronos_list_checkpoints, chronos_diff, chronos_rollback, in JSON with
status, created, id, hash, diff, stat, restored and safety), the rollback
takes a safety checkpoint first and then writes the tree back with `git
read-tree --reset -u`, and /chronos with no argument lists, /chronos diff ID
shows one change and /chronos rollback ID [--no-clean] restores one. The
section's settings are the original's: automatic checkpoints before a
modifying call, the ignored patterns, how many checkpoints are listed, and
whether a restore deletes files created since the checkpoint.

Left out: the Hermes host plumbing. The original's hooks are Hermes's
pre_tool_call, post_tool_call and transform_tool_result and its approval
directive for a model-initiated rollback; here one hook on Nodecode's :tool
point runs around each tool call -- it decides by tool name whether to
checkpoint, and it appends the same recovery hint to a result that reads as
a failure, without the approve/deny round trip, because a restore here always
takes its safety checkpoint first and can be undone. The dashboard backend
(FastAPI routes mounted for the Desktop pane) and the Desktop timeline
(React) have no Nodecode equivalent and are not carried: the operator's own
surface is /chronos, which lists, diffs and restores in text. Compaction of
the shadow repository past a checkpoint count is left to git (gc.auto=0 in
the cell's own runs, so no git command of the operator's is slowed by it).
